{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"agent monitoring and evaluation distinction agent monitoring and evaluation distinction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","fileName":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-27 12:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[AI Agent Observability and Evaluation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Agent Observability and Evaluation","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"agent monitoring and evaluation distinction agent monitoring and evaluation distinction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","fileName":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction","heading":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Monitoring asks whether an agent workflow is fast, available, failing, or expensive. Evaluation asks whether its output is correct, grounded, instruction-following, safe, and useful. The two answer different operational questions.\n\nA workflow can have low latency and no infrastructure errors while consistently producing poor recommendations. Conversely, a useful result can arrive through an unreliable process. Responsible operation therefore combines service health and cost signals with explicit quality and safety checks rather than treating successful execution as successful reasoning.","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Agent Observability and Evaluation","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"agent monitoring and evaluation distinction agent monitoring and evaluation distinction","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","fileName":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Agent Monitoring and Evaluation Distinction","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["AI Agent Observability and Evaluation","agenticaifordevopsengineers.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}